 "researcher_notes": "A Michigan Public Service Commission order dated November 19, 2020 (Case U-20618) approved Consumers Energy's 36 inch Mid-Michigan Pipeline, about 56 miles between Chelsea and Ovid, replacing the 20 inch Line 100A. The application was filed August 23, 2019. The order estimated cost at 550 million US dollars. A news article from the approval period (WKAR) gives the same figures. A Pipeline and Gas Journal article from November 2024 says the company finished the line, replacing 55 miles of 20 inch pipe in Clinton, Shiawassee, Ingham, Livingston and Washtenaw counties. Length staged as 56 miles from the order; completed length reported as 55 miles. The 2024 article cites a cost of 1.5 billion dollars, which conflicts with the 550 million estimate; the cost staged is the order estimate and should be checked. No existing GEM row for Consumers Energy, CMS Energy, Line 100A or Mid-Michigan was found in the roster (only DTE lines and Saginaw Trail, a different line). It adds well over 25 km of new pipe on a partly rerouted path, so it passes the length rule. Owner style: entity tool gave only a stem match for Consumers Energy Co, so the plain name is kept; parent CMS Energy Corp is an exact gazetteer match. No route researched; no official GIS checked. Start year 2024 is from the completion article. Confidence high."
}